  data:  # 452e
    kind: invariant  # 452e
    title: "last_stop_check.json: one location, one writer"  # 452e
    status: violated  # 452e
    priority: 1  # 452e
    parent:  # 452e
    tags:  # 452e
    - governance  # 452e
    - agent_state_recovery  # 452e
    - stop_hook  # 452e
    before: []  # 452e
    duplicate_of: []  # 452e
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 452e
    pr_ref:  # 452e
    description: "Discovered during 2026-04-10 session orientation. The agent-facing state file `last_stop_check.json` violates two related invariants that together cause agent state-recovery confusion. The user (jgstern) correctly flagged this as significant and recalled prior work on a similar problem.\n\n## Historical context\n\n- WI-bulif (2026-03-05, \"Move last_stop_check.json out of git tree\") intended to relocate the file to `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/` to eliminate git noise. Closed DONE via commit `84a63c8f`.\n- A follow-up commit `011bc8ac0` (\"fix: move last_stop_check.json into guidance_log to unbreak circuit breaker\") refined the target path to `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guidance_log/last_stop_check.json`.\n- WI-jigig (\"AGENTS.md: update last_stop_check notes more frequently\") closed DONE, adding the \"Keep notes fresh\" jq snippet in the recover-state-playbook.\n- Today (2026-04-10) I discovered two loose ends that weren't closed by any of those items.\n\n## Facet 1 — vestigial file still in git HEAD\n\n```\ngit ls-files .agent/last_stop_check.json\n  → .agent/last_stop_check.json  (tracked)\ngit cat-file -e HEAD:.agent/last_stop_check.json\n  → EXISTS_IN_HEAD\nstat .agent/last_stop_check.json\n  → mtime 2026-03-17 01:02\ncat .agent/last_stop_check.json | jq .last_completed_utc\n  → \"2026-03-05T18:00:00Z\"  (36 days old)\n```\n\n`.gitignore` line 34 has `.agent/last_stop_check.json` but gitignore does not untrack already-tracked files. The move commit `84a63c8f` added the ignore entry and updated all writers but forgot to `git rm --cached` the old path. Result: the file persists in the tree with stale content.\n\nAgent impact: in orientation today I ran `cat .agent/last_stop_check.json` because the file path is still intuitive and was documented in older commit bodies. I got 36-day-old content and mistakenly concluded the stop hook had been broken since March. This is exactly the confusion the user warned about.\n\n## Facet 2 — canonical file has stale last_completed_utc despite fresh mtime\n\n```\nstat ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guidance_log/last_stop_check.json\n  → mtime 2026-04-10 17:26 (today)\njq . ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guidance_log/last_stop_check.json\n  → last_completed_utc: \"2026-03-30T22:20:04Z\"  (11 days old)\n  → notes: \"Session 04/10 FINAL: 12 code PRs merged...\"  (today)\n  → guidance_file: \"stop_guidance_04102026_2126.md\"  (today)\n```\n\nThe file is being written today, but `last_completed_utc` contradicts the notes and guidance_file fields.\n\nRoot cause: `.agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh` has NO writer for `last_completed_utc`. It only READS the field at line 309 to compute `ELAPSED_MIN` for Path 2 (cooldown) vs Path 3 (reflection) selection. The jq merge at lines 288-294 writes only `guidance_file`, `bakeoff_convergence`, `bakeoff_session_path`, `bakeoff_session_type`.\n\nThe only writer in code is the python snippet at `.agent/stop_reflect.md` lines 85-128, which is plain-language instruction for the agent to execute manually at the end of each reflection cycle.\n\nSeparately, the \"Keep notes fresh\" jq snippet at `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/recover-state-playbook.md` lines 20-26 writes only the `notes` field — it explicitly does not touch `last_completed_utc`. So agents following that playbook refresh notes but leave the timestamp stuck.\n\nSelf-referential gating: Path 3 reflection path in stop_logic.sh only fires when `ELAPSED_MIN >= 30`, where ELAPSED_MIN is derived from `last_completed_utc`. Once the value gets stuck, every subsequent hook fire reads the same stale value and computes a huge ELAPSED_MIN, continuing to fire Path 3 (or Path 1 if TODOs exist). The Path 2 cooldown path, which exists specifically to suppress reflection-spam on rapid consecutive hook fires, has been dead code for 11 days.\n\n## Violated invariant\n\n**INVARIANT: `last_stop_check.json` lives at exactly one filesystem location, and the set of code locations that write each field is exactly {stop hook} — not {stop hook, stop_reflect.md snippet, recover-state-playbook snippet, manual ad-hoc jq commands}.**\n\nBoth facets violate this invariant:\n- Facet 1: two filesystem locations exist (vestigial .agent/ path + canonical ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guidance_log/ path).\n- Facet 2: the canonical file has multiple inconsistent writers for different fields, none of which maintain the full schema atomically. `last_completed_utc` has no automatic writer at all.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\n1. **Delete vestigial file (Facet 1)** — `git rm .agent/last_stop_check.json` + commit. `.gitignore` entry is already in place so nothing re-tracks it. Non-governance, can ship as a normal PR.\n\n2. **Unify writers (Facet 2)** — Make `stop_logic.sh` the single writer for all persistent fields. Extend the jq merge at lines 288-294 to also set `last_completed_utc = now` when Path 3 (reflection) fires. Semantic change: the field becomes \"last time hook told agent to reflect\" rather than \"last time agent finished reflecting\" — deterministic, hook-maintained, no reliance on agent discipline. Delete the manual python snippet from `.agent/stop_reflect.md`. Update `recover-state-playbook.md` \"Keep notes fresh\" jq snippet with a warning that only `notes` should be touched manually — all other fields come from the hook. This touches governance files (`.agent/hooks/**` and `.agent/stop_reflect.md`), so the change must be proposed here and approved before a PR is opened.\n\n3. **Audit for other drifted fields** — `last_pr`, `last_pr_num`, `last_pr_state`, `current_branch`, `pending_hard_todos`, `pending_soft_todos` may also be stale. Either the hook should refresh them deterministically, or the schema should shrink to only fields the hook can maintain. Investigate after facet 2 fix.\n\n## Why this is high priority\n\nAgents rely on `last_stop_check.json` as the single source of truth for state recovery after context compaction. When that source contradicts itself (notes say \"today\", timestamp says \"11 days ago\") or when two copies exist with different values, the agent makes incorrect decisions about what work is in flight, what just merged, and what needs attention. Today I spent ~10 minutes investigating a non-bug (thought stop hook had been broken since March) that was actually just file confusion. Every future agent orientation risks the same failure mode until this is fixed."  # 452e
    fields:  # 452e
      statement: "last_stop_check.json lives at exactly one filesystem location, and the set of code locations that write each field is exactly {stop hook} — not {stop hook, stop_reflect.md snippet, recover-state-playbook snippet, manual ad-hoc jq commands}"  # 452e
      root_cause: "Commit 84a63c8f moved the file out of .agent/ but did not git-rm the old path, and never unified writers. WI-bulif closed as done without enforcing the 'one location, one writer' invariant as an acceptance criterion."  # 452e
